  <story>
    <asA>developer</asA>
    <iWant>architectural decisions automatically extracted and stored as decision nodes with full lineage</iWant>
    <soThat>every "why" is captured, connected to the requirements it addresses, and traceable to the code that implements it</soThat>
    <tasks>
      <task id="1" ac="1,4">Implement decision extraction from architecture documents
        <subtask>Create /home/ubuntu/scripts/lib/extract-decisions.mjs for parsing architecture session output and extracting discrete decisions</subtask>
        <subtask>Identify decision patterns: technology choices (we chose X over Y), pattern selections (using the repository pattern), API design choices (REST over GraphQL), data model decisions (single table vs multi-table)</subtask>
        <subtask>For each extracted decision, generate an ADR-format article with sections: Context, Options Considered, Chosen Option, Rationale, Consequences</subtask>
        <subtask>Generate unique nodeId: decisions/{project-slug}--{decision-slug}</subtask>
        <subtask>Set frontmatter: type: adr, phase: solutioning, status: active, tags derived from domain context</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="2" ac="2">Create DERIVED_FROM edges to requirements
        <subtask>For each decision, identify which requirements it addresses by matching against existing requirement nodes in Memgraph (semantic search + keyword matching)</subtask>
        <subtask>Add Derived From section with [[wikilinks]] to matched requirement articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Run graph-sync.mjs to create DERIVED_FROM edges (weight 0.7) from decision nodes to requirement nodes</subtask>
        <subtask>If no matching requirements found, log a warning (decision exists without traceability)</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="3" ac="3,6">Create placeholder code articles with INFORMS edges
        <subtask>Analyze each decision to infer what code files it implies (e.g., JWT auth implies an auth component, a JWT utility, a token store)</subtask>
        <subtask>Create placeholder articles in knowledge/code/ with status: suggested, maturity: 0.1, and Purpose describing expected implementation</subtask>
        <subtask>Add Informs section in decision article with [[wikilinks]] to placeholder code articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Run graph-sync.mjs to create INFORMS edges (weight 0.3) from decision nodes to placeholder code nodes</subtask>
        <subtask>When Dev agent creates actual code files during story compilation, detect matching placeholders and transition: status suggested to active, update maturity, preserve INFORMS edge</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="4" ac="5">Implement conflict detection
        <subtask>When a new decision is extracted, query Memgraph for existing decisions in same domain (same tags, similar topic via vector similarity > 0.8)</subtask>
        <subtask>If potential conflict found, use Knowledge Compiler agent to assess whether the two decisions genuinely contradict</subtask>
        <subtask>If confirmed conflict: create CONFLICTS_WITH edge (weight 0.9, bidirectional) between decision nodes</subtask>
        <subtask>Add Conflicts With section in both decision articles with [[wikilinks]]</subtask>
        <subtask>Log conflict in knowledge/log.md and add entry to knowledge/system/pending-work.md for human review</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="5" ac="1">Integrate into pre-dev compilation flow
        <subtask>Hook extract-decisions.mjs into pre-dev compilation step (Story 4.1) for article types: architecture, tech-spec, api-spec, data-model, adr</subtask>
        <subtask>Handle architecture revisions: diff against existing decision nodes, update changed, add new, mark obsolete as status: superseded</subtask>
        <subtask>Run impact propagation (Story 3.5) after decision updates to flag downstream code nodes</subtask>
        <subtask>Update knowledge/index.md with all new decision and placeholder code articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Log extraction results in knowledge/log.md: architecture nodeId, decision count, conflict count, placeholder count</subtask>
      </task>
    </tasks>
  </story>

  <acceptanceCriteria>
    <criterion id="1">When an Architect agent session produces or revises technical documents (architecture, tech-spec, api-spec, data-model), the compilation step extracts explicit decisions as separate articles in knowledge/decisions/</criterion>
    <criterion id="2">Each decision article has DERIVED_FROM edges to the requirement nodes it addresses (linking back to Story 4.2 requirement decomposition)</criterion>
    <criterion id="3">Each decision article has INFORMS edges to placeholder code articles created with status: suggested representing code that the architecture implies will exist but has not been written yet</criterion>
    <criterion id="4">Decision articles include: context, options considered, chosen option, rationale, and consequences following the ADR format</criterion>
    <criterion id="5">If a new decision contradicts an existing decision in the same domain, a CONFLICTS_WITH edge is created between the two decision nodes</criterion>
    <criterion id="6">When the Dev agent later creates actual code files, the placeholder status: suggested articles transition to status: active and the INFORMS edges are preserved</criterion>
  </acceptanceCriteria>

