  <constraints>
    <constraint type="architecture">Decision nodes use ADR format (Context, Options Considered, Chosen Option, Rationale, Consequences). This is a well-established pattern for architecture decision records.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Placeholder code articles have status: suggested and maturity: 0.1. They represent architectural intent before implementation. When actual code is created, placeholders transition to status: active — the INFORMS edge is preserved.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Conflict detection uses both structural (tag overlap) and semantic (vector similarity > 0.8) matching. The Knowledge Compiler agent makes the final determination of genuine contradiction.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">CONFLICTS_WITH edges are bidirectional (weight 0.9). Both conflicting decision articles get Conflicts With sections with mutual [[wikilinks]]. Conflicts are logged to pending-work.md for human review.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">Requires Story 4.1 (Document Generation Compilation Hook) and Story 4.2 (Requirement Decomposition) — decisions link back to requirement nodes via DERIVED_FROM.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">Requires Epic 1 complete (Memgraph with vector index for semantic search, graph-sync) and Story 3.5 (Impact Propagation Engine).</constraint>
  </constraints>

